.TH GAMERX-THEME 1 "2026-05-28" "GamerX OS" "GamerX OS Manual"
.SH NAME
gamerx-theme \- single source of truth for GamerX OS theming
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gamerx-theme
.RI { show | get | set | list | apply | reset }
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gamerx-theme
is the only tool that should write GamerX OS theme state. The Welcome app and
GamerX Settings call this CLI; users may call it directly. State lives in
.B ~/.config/gamerx/state.toml
and is applied by renderers shipped in
.BR /usr/share/gamerx-theme/renderers/ .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Print all current state values.
.TP
.BI "get " key
Print one value.
.TP
.BI "set " "key value"
Change one value and re-apply. Use
.B --no-apply
to save only.
.TP
.BI "list " kind
List available values for a kind:
.BR palettes ,
.BR densities ,
.BR animations ,
.BR launchers ,
.BR bars ,
.BR notifications .
.TP
.B apply
Re-render every config from current state.
.TP
.B reset
Reset to factory defaults.
.SH KEYS
palette, density, animation, launcher, bar, notification, icon_theme, wallpaper.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/gamerx/state.toml
User state file.
.TP
.B /usr/share/gamerx/palettes/
System palettes from
.BR gamerx-branding .
.TP
.B ~/.config/gamerx/palettes/
User-imported palettes (override system).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR matugen (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
